# Ashby — Org-Wide Config

API plumbing shared across all jobs and skills. These rarely change.

## Sources (candidate attribution)
| Source | ID |
|--------|-----|
| WAAS (Work at a Startup) | `<your-waas-source-id>` |
| Applied (direct) | `<your-applied-source-id>` |
| Chrome Extension (sourced) | `<your-chrome-ext-source-id>` |
| Jack and Jill | `<your-jj-source-id>` |

## Archive Reasons
| Reason | ID |
|--------|-----|
| Not a good match | `<your-archive-reason-id>` |

### Archiving an application

**Use `application_change_stage` with the Archived stage ID, not `application_update`.**

To archive a candidate, call `application_change_stage(applicationId, interviewStageId: "<Archived stage ID from recruit-config/jobs/>", archiveReasonId: <reason ID>)`.

⚠️ **Footgun:** `application_update` with `{"status": "Archived", "archiveReasonId": ...}` returns HTTP 200 success but **silently no-ops on the status field** — `currentInterviewStage` and `archiveReason` are unchanged. The only thing that moves is `updatedAt`. Always use `application_change_stage` and verify the response has `currentInterviewStage.title == "Archived"` and a populated `archiveReason`.

## Interview Feedback

Use these when submitting interview feedback via `application_feedback_submit`.
Slack, user IDs, and feedback form IDs are in `user.md`.

### Fields
| Path | Type | Values |
|------|------|--------|
| `overall_recommendation` | ValueSelect | `4` = Strong Yes, `3` = Yes, `2` = No, `1` = Strong No |
| `feedback` | RichText | `{"type": "PlainText", "value": "your text"}` |

### Rules
1. **Always attach feedback to an interview event.** Look up the interview schedule for the application (`interview_schedule_list`), find the relevant `interviewEventId`, and pass it to the submit call. Never submit standalone feedback when an interview event exists.
2. **Never use `candidate_create_note` as a substitute for feedback.** Notes and feedback are different things in Ashby. Feedback has a score and is attached to an interview; notes are freeform comments on the candidate.
3. **Workflow:** `interview_schedule_list(applicationId)` → get `interviewEvents[].id` → `application_feedback_submit(applicationId, formDefinitionId, interviewEventId, feedbackForm, userId)`

## Email Style

**No hard line wrapping.** Write each paragraph as a single continuous line — let the email client handle wrapping. Never insert newlines within a paragraph for formatting. Only use newlines between paragraphs.

## Gmail

Hiring manager email is in `user.md`.

### Draft tool
**Always use `mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__gmail_create_draft`** (not `mcp__gmail-drafts__gmail_create_draft`) when creating email drafts. Set `contentType: "text/html"` and wrap the body in `<p>` tags with `<br><br>` between paragraphs. The `gmail-drafts` tool only supports `text/plain`, which causes Gmail to hard-wrap lines at ~78 characters per RFC 2822 — making emails look broken.

To send a draft created with `mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__gmail_create_draft`, use `mcp__gmail-drafts__gmail_send_draft` with the `draftId` returned.

### Known noise senders
See `user.md` for the full list of noise senders to exclude from inbox checks.
